The attached image illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan. Panel (A) shows a Transmission Electron Microscopy image, revealing spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface, emphasizing their nanoscale (scale bar 50 nm). Panel (B) displays a diameter distribution histogram obtained via dynamic light scattering, indicating a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter consistently between 75 and 80 nm, affirming the uniform size crucial for their function as vaccine adjuvants.

The image significantly contributes to vaccine development by showcasing the precise physical characteristics (70-80 nm size, spherical, irregular morphology) of Nano-11, which are optimized for efficient uptake by dendritic cells and enhanced antigen delivery. This controlled size and structure are critical for designing next-generation adjuvants that can effectively activate immune responses and ensure a favorable safety profile, making Nano-11 a promising candidate for prophylactic vaccines.